# Release payload — published as GitHub Release assets, never committed.
# parts/ is ~7.9 GB and part_bundles/ ~7.8 GB; several bundles exceed GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file hard limit, so a `git add -A` here produces a push that is
# rejected only after uploading gigabytes.
Dist_Repo/v2/parts/
Dist_Repo/v2/part_bundles/

# 156 MB, also over the file limit. Published on the lib-v2-index release,
# which is what `search_index_url` in the manifest points at.
Dist_Repo/v2/lib_search.sqlite

# Build-run output, not part of the published index.
Dist_Repo/validation/
reports/

# One JSON per contract, rewritten in full by every `libcontract build`. At 399
# contracts it was 6 MB a rebuild and worth having in git for the diff; at
# 7,111 it is 131 MB a rebuild for a diff nobody reads at that size. Nothing
# consumes it — the app reads contracts/contracts.json and the per-part summary
# lives in contracts/contract_index.json, both of which stay committed.
Dist_Repo/v2/contracts/parts/
